Third-party components and data in this repository

0. Repository ancestry: Karylcode/VRoid-MCP
   https://github.com/Karylcode/VRoid-MCP
   Local fork baseline: 9b264d3ad3a33bea2e18e91a0476e395246a6be6.
   The 9b264d3 baseline did not include a licence; its inherited implementation
   was replaced before publication. Later upstream commit baaa94e, published
   with MIT licence, is the source for portions of the ordinary-edit export,
   part operations, attached-session and isolation adaptations. Copyright (c)
   2026 Karylcode. See licenses/karylcode-upstream-20261023.txt and LICENSING.md.

1. vroid_mcp/data/preset_labels/
   Preset labels and the thumbnail-addressing algorithm are adapted from
   brainrom/vroid-studio-mcp, Copyright (c) 2026 Ilya Chelyadin and
   vroid-studio-mcp contributors, MIT, commit
   a6b0719d01fa6cac9a857956907243d9916390b2.
   See vroid_mcp/data/preset_labels/LICENSE and NOTICE.

2. vroid_mcp/data/parameter_labels/, data/color_state/, data/capture_quality/,
   data/capture_framing/
   Same upstream project and license; each directory carries its own LICENSE
   and NOTICE with the exact files and commit it came from.

3. frida-il2cpp-bridge (npm, MIT) is consumed at runtime through
   node_modules; it is not vendored in this repository.

4. frida (PyPI) and mcp (PyPI) are declared dependencies; their licenses are
   their own.

5. mcjo79/vroid-mcp
   https://github.com/mcjo79/vroid-mcp
   Reference revision: 0dc7d5eb3cf27f7f943713960cac1b65f479a876.
   Copyright (c) 2026 mcjo79 and vroid-mcp contributors, MIT.
   The complete source LICENSE is retained by file-level copy in
   licenses/mcjo79-0dc7d5e.txt. MIGRATION.md records all 53 source tools,
   the source files used for each adaptation, destination modules and evidence.
   Adaptations include native edit and export workflows, image processing,
   camera control, preset catalog storage and category framing. The target
   retains its Python/Frida backend; the source BepInEx/Harmony/HTTP control
   framework is not incorporated. The adopted integration is BunnyBlack
   feat/mcjo79-capability-migration at c19aeff. The Steam 2.16.0 assembly
   hash from that fork is not admitted.

6. shamsievartyom/VRoid-Character-MCP
   https://github.com/shamsievartyom/VRoid-Character-MCP
   Reference revision: cb71a749f7045176154850a121a0d5081197ec37.
   Copyright (c) 2026 Shamsiev Artem. MIT, as a fork of this repository.
   Adapted clothing-template tools, InnerTop and other clothing texture
   editor modes, compact canvas IDs, capture_review(include_images=false),
   client_repl.py, vroid_mcp/local_comparison.py and the reference workflow
   in vroid_mcp/workflow.py.

VRoid Studio, its assemblies and the VRM format are not distributed here.
Character assets, textures and Blender files produced during development stay
local and are excluded by .gitignore.
